# NOTICE: the OV02C10 component of Tessera's Screen camera

This folder adds the OmniVision OV02C10 to esp_video_camera: a sensor driver for Espressif's esp_cam_sensor and an
image tuning for esp_video's ISP pipeline. It was written and first tried on a Guition JC8012P4A1 V3 by Jeroen Peters
(@Heronimonimo). The plugin as a whole is distributed under GPL-3.0-only; the notices below stay with their files.

## Where the files come from

* `ov02c10_settings.h`, `ov02c10_regs.h`, `ov02c10_types.h`, `ov02c10.h`: Guition's OV02C10 driver files, as their
  own copy of esp_cam_sensor in the JC4880P443C firmware SDK publishes them (seen at
  github.com/wegi1/ESP32P4-JC4880P443C-I-W, `1-Demo/idf_examples/components/espressif__esp_cam_sensor/sensors/ov02c10`).
  They carry Espressif's `SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0` header, kept as it is. They came here through
  github.com/sullb/esphome-p4-csi-camera (MIT License, below; copied 2026-10-18), which changed a few start values: 23
  lines of the register tables differ from Guition's, and the 1288x728 table that is used is the same. `ov02c10_regs.h`
  lost an unused OV5640 define on 2026-10-20.
* `ov02c10_sensor.c` and `ov02c10_compat.h`: sullb's version of Guition's driver, in the structure of Espressif's
  esp_cam_sensor drivers (Apache-2.0, the SPDX header is kept). Changed on 2026-10-19, as its header says: exposure,
  analog gain and orientation on the sensor's own registers, the OV5640 registers removed, the chip id checked.
* Linux's drivers/media/i2c/ov02c10.c (GPL-2.0) was read as a reference for what the registers mean (exposure at
  0x3501, analog gain at 0x3508, mirror and flip in 0x3820, the window offsets and limits). No code and no register
  table was copied from it.
* `ipa/ov02c10_p4_eco5.json` and `ipa/ov02c10_p4_eco4.json`: image tuning derived from Espressif's
  `sc2336_default_p4_eco4.json` (esp_cam_sensor, Apache-2.0) under the name OV02C10, with a wider white balance search
  and a neutral saturation. The eco5 file adds the black level and the gamma of Espressif's rev3 tunings
  (`sc2336_default_p4_eco5.json`, `os02n10_default_p4_eco5.json`) and white balance gain scales; the eco4 file has
  neither, since older chips correct no black level. `ipa/CMakeLists.txt`, `ipa/project_include.cmake` and
  `__init__.py` are this plugin's own.

